  "title": "When something goes wrong on the retreat",
  "sourceHash": "sha256:c1448051d110a169829c59d80785bb9ef78159ebfc9b287bedbcfb0646a1d265",
  "outline": [
    {
      "heading": "Who decides",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "First of all, agree who makes decisions on the retreat if something goes wrong.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "A guest who feels unwell",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "The guest form already knows about their health and a close contact.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "A difficult guest",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Someone disrupts sessions, argues with the group, breaks the rules.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "A booking or the journey falls through",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "The venue mixed up the dates, the transfer did not come, a flight was cancelled.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Weather and natural events",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Heavy rain cancels a walk, heat cancels a practice in the sun.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "What to tell the group",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Briefly, truthfully and at once: what happened, what is already being done, what changes in the programme.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Afterwards",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Write down what happened and how it was solved — the same day.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  ],
